          wrongTurn: 'The wrong turn is treating observation as watching someone use an interface. Most of what you are there for happens around it: the setting, the interruptions, the other things they are doing.',
          tradeoff: 'Recording the environment produces messy notes that are harder to summarise. They are the notes that explain the behaviour.',
